/* ── MODERN FOCUSED, ROOMS PAGE: THE BOARDS CARD'S SURFACE (2026-09-24) ─────────────────
   Requested: "make this div bg the same bg as the boards page md-workspace on modern focused".

   THE BOARDS PAGE'S `.md-workspace` PAINTS NOTHING -- measured, it computes to
   `background: none` with a transparent colour. The surface that reads as the boards page in
   Focused is `.ub-boards-page__boards-section`, and it gets it from `$focus-boards-bg`, the
   shared frosted-glass token this file already hands to the focused home page's Boards card and
   to the Extras page for exactly this "match the boards card" purpose (see `.md-extras-page`
   above). So this reuses the token rather than copying the two gradients out of the inspector,
   and the four surfaces cannot drift.

   THE BACKDROP FILTER COMES WITH IT, and that is not scope creep: every layer in
   `$focus-boards-bg` is translucent, so what the panel actually looks like is decided as much by
   what it blurs behind it as by the gradient itself. `.md-main--org` was on blur(22px)
   saturate(1.35) against the boards card's blur(14px) saturate(1.3); leaving that alone would
   have applied the right gradient and still not matched.
