}

/* ...AND IT STAYS PUT FROM 1024px DOWN (requested 2026-09-24: "Rooms page on 1024px and
   smaller, the content is shifting up on the page -> prevent that from happening").
   THE JUMP IS THE BASE WORKSPACE'S TOP MARGIN GOING AWAY. `.md-workspace` is `margin: 40px
   auto` at desktop widths and 0 at 1024 and below, and its padding steps 40 -> 52 -> 40 across
   the same range. Measured on this page: the switcher sat at y=174 at 1280 and 1100, then 134
   at 1024 and 1000, then 146 at 950 -- a 40px jump up and a 12px partial recovery, none of it
   this page's own doing.
   The gentle block in app.scss absorbs the same loss for the pages it covers by adding 52px of
   shell padding at this breakpoint; these pages take the shell's padding to 0, so they had
   nothing to absorb it with.
   BOTH VALUES ARE PINNED, not just the margin: restoring only the margin would have left the
   950px step's 12px of extra padding, so the page would have stopped jumping up and started
   drifting down instead. With both fixed the sum is 26 + 0 + 40 + 40 = the same y at every
   width in this band.
   FLOORED AT 901px on purpose. At 900 and below the account rail stops being a fixed panel and
   becomes an in-flow band above the page (app.scss), so everything below it moves by design --
   that is a layout change, not a shift to pin. */
@media (max-width: 1024px) and (min-width: 901px) {
  /* MODERN ONLY since 2026-10-01: Basic's org pages take no top gap at any width above 900px
     (_classic-home.scss, "ORG PAGES: NO TOP GAP"), and this rule's id weight would override that. */
  body.ll-view-modern.ll-layout-focused #content:has(.md-shell--org:not(.md-shell--org-directory)) .md-workspace {
    margin-top: 40px !important;
    padding-top: 40px !important;
  }
}
