body.ll-layout-focused .nb-section__title:not(.nb-section__title--inline) {
  /* DARKER than the gentle pill it replaces (requested): the denim roughly doubles at
     both stops and the white top sheen is pulled back from 0.35 to 0.22, so the wash
     reads as a filled pill rather than a tint. Same three-stop construction and the same
     geometry — only the densities move.
     MEASURED, not estimated. The bottom stop (0.34 denim over the card) resolves to
     rgb(188, 209, 239) and carries $la-navy at 7.80:1; the midpoint stop (0.18) resolves
     to rgb(215, 227, 245) at 9.35:1. The bottom of the gradient is therefore the worst
     case, not an average, and it clears both the 4.5:1 AA floor and AAA's 7:1 for normal
     text. Deepening much past this starts eating the AAA margin — re-measure before
     doing so, because the ink is what has to keep up. */
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.22) 0%, rgba(76, 134, 216, 0.18) 35%, rgba(76, 134, 216, 0.34) 100%);
  box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4), 0 2px 12px rgba(76, 134, 216, 0.22);
}

