/* ORGANIZATIONS PAGE WITH THE BASIC RAIL (2026-09-23).
   `templates/organizations.hbs` renders <Dashboard::ClassicRail /> as a DIRECT CHILD of
   `.md-shell`, which is the element carrying the page gradient -- that is what stretches the
   background across the whole page instead of leaving the rail on bare page background.

   `.md-shell` is already `display: flex; flex-direction: column !important`, so Basic only has
   to turn it into a row. No wrapper element is introduced, on purpose: `.md-shell >
   .md-workspace` is a direct-child selector carrying the workspace's `flex` and `min-height`,
   and a wrapper would silently detach both -- changing Modern's layout to deliver a
   Basic-only feature.

   `!important` THROUGHOUT, matching not fighting: every base declaration overridden here
   (`.md-shell`'s `flex-direction` and `padding-top`, `.md-shell > .md-workspace`'s `flex`,
   `.md-shell--org-directory .md-workspace`'s `margin-top`) is itself `!important`, and
   `!important` is not beaten by specificity alone.

   THE INSETS ARE THE HOME PAGE'S, not new ones (requested: "the same position on the page as
   it does on the home page", and then the same distance from the left edge). `.ch-page` below
   is what positions the rail on the Basic dashboard, and its padding is copied here whole --
   `80px 28px 24px`, plus its two top steps (44px at <=1024px, 48px stacked at <=900px) and its
   22px side inset at <=767px. The 28px left is what puts the rail the same distance in from
   the page edge on both pages; without it the shell has no side padding and the rail sat flush
   against the viewport.

   THE BASE IS A SHORTHAND AND THE BREAKPOINTS ARE LONGHANDS, copying `.ch-page`'s own
   discipline (see the note at its <=900px block): a shorthand in a media query would reset the
   side padding every time it only meant to change the top.

   The workspace's own 20px top margin is zeroed in this layout so the rail and the content
   share one top edge, the way `.ch-page`'s two columns do -- AND SO IS ITS 40px TOP PADDING
   (2026-09-24, requested: "move the organizations page content up on the page"). Zeroing the
   margin alone did not finish the job the sentence above describes: measured at 1280, the rail
   started at y=126 and the org hero at y=166, because the base `.md-workspace` padding still
   sat inside the card. With both gone the two share a top edge for real.
   THE CONTENT KEEPS ITS INSET -- `.md-hero--org` carries its own top padding (20px, and 28px
   above 1200px where more room was asked for earlier the same week), so removing the
   workspace's padding moves the block up without pushing the title against the card edge. */
/* `.la-system-settings .la-main` ADDED 2026-10-10, when System Settings gained the rail. Its
   page has no `.md-shell`; `main.la-main` is the flex column the rail and the workspace share,
   and `.la-system-settings` appears only in templates/system-settings.hbs, so nothing else moves.
   `--board-picker` ADDED 2026-10-09, when that page gained the same rail. Stated as a second
   selector rather than generalised to `.md-shell:has(> .ch-rail)`, which would read better but
   would ALSO newly match templates/organization.hbs -- it carries `md-shell--org` (not
   `--org-directory`) and mounts a rail, so a generic selector would change that page's layout
   too, which nobody asked for. */
body.ll-view-basic .md-shell--org-directory,
body.ll-view-basic .md-shell--board-picker {
  flex-direction: row !important;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 24px;
  padding: 80px 28px 24px !important;
}

/* SYSTEM SETTINGS: the same row, its own top. Its page is `.la-wrapper`, a FIXED full-viewport
   overlay that starts at y=0 under the app header, where the shells above flow BELOW it. The rail
   sits header + 24px down on Organizations at every width (measured 2026-10-10: 70+24=94 from
   768px up, 114+24=138 at 767px and below), so this main's top is header + 36: the 24px gap plus
   the rail's own -12px top margin. The header height is 70px / 114px either side of 768px; the
   <=767px step is in the media block below. */
body.ll-view-basic .la-system-settings .la-main {
