/* NO TOP PADDING ON THE DIRECTORY'S HERO (2026-09-24, requested: "basic view: organizations -
   remove the top padding from the hero"). The header is `.md-hero.md-hero--dashboard` and takes
   `padding: 28px 2px 10px` from the base `.md-hero`; with the workspace's own padding now gone
   (above), that 28px was the last thing holding "My Organizations" below the rail's top edge.
   `padding-top` ALONE, not the shorthand: the 2px sides and the 10px bottom are the header's own
   rhythm and were not asked about, and a shorthand here would silently reset both.
   NOT `.md-hero--org`, which is a DIFFERENT element -- the org DETAIL pages' header, whose top
   padding was deliberately widened on large screens a few days ago. `:not(.md-hero--org)` keeps
