   Below 1024px this is already 0 from `@media (max-width: 1024px) { .md-hero--dashboard }`, so
   this rule only does work on wider screens.
   `!important` MATCHED, not added: the base `.md-hero` shorthand carries one (app.scss:47657),
   and specificity alone does not beat it -- this landed with no visible effect until the flag
   was added, measured at 28px either way. */
body.ll-view-basic .md-shell:has(> .ch-rail) .md-hero--dashboard:not(.md-hero--org) {
