/* BESIDE THE RAIL, EVERY PAGE TITLE STARTS ON THE CONTENT LINE, AT EVERY WIDTH (2026-10-01,
   requested: fix the header title spacing on Account, Reports and the org directory -- it sat
   40-55px below the rail and jumped 8-20px at 1024).
   THE RULE ABOVE WAS THE DIRECTORY'S ALONE; it now covers every Basic page whose rail is a direct
   child of its shell (the account section, Reports, the directory), so their header has no top
   padding there either. The org pages' header is excluded: its padding (below, "MORE BREATHING
   ROOM") is the gap between the tab strip or switcher and the title, not space above the page.
   AND NO TITLE MARGIN: at <=1024 the shared dashboard hero turns into a flex column and gives
   its title `margin-top: 2rem` to clear the tour chip (app.scss), which that block itself now
   pins `position: fixed`; the account section then takes 11px below 901, and Reports 12px.
