body.ll-view-basic .md-shell:has(> .ch-rail) .md-hero--dashboard .md-hero__title {
  margin-top: 0 !important;
}

/* FOCUSED HIDES THE DIRECTORY'S HEADER (2026-09-24, requested: "basic view: focused. Hide the
   hero and subtitle"). Same move Focused already makes on Extras and Reports, where the page
   title is carried by the nav you arrived through rather than repeated at the top of the page.
   THE SUBTITLE GOES, THE HEADING STAYS FOR ASSISTIVE TECH. `.md-hero__sub` is decorative prose
   ("Choose an organization to manage or view...") and is simply removed. The `<h1>` is this
   page's ONLY heading (templates/organizations.hbs:23), so `display: none` on the hero would
   leave the document with no title at all -- on a product whose users include screen-reader and
   switch users, that is a regression, not a tidy-up. The visually-hidden block below takes it
   off screen while leaving it in the accessibility tree, which is what "hide" means here.
   WRITTEN OUT RATHER THAN `@include aac-sr-only`: that mixin is defined in app.scss, which this
   partial is `@use`d BY and cannot see -- the include compiled to "Undefined mixin" and took the
   whole stylesheet down (dev server 500). Same declarations as the mixin (app.scss:28763), kept
   in step by this note rather than by an import this file cannot have.
   GENTLE IS UNTOUCHED, and so is the hero's padding rule above -- that still governs Gentle,
