   `color` rather than taking a lighter one. Dimming it is the obvious way to make it secondary
   and it is how AA gets quietly undone -- the tab colour is chosen per scheme to clear 4.5:1,
   and any alpha applied here would drop below that in whichever scheme is tighter, invisibly.
   Smaller and lighter reads as secondary without touching contrast. */
.ch-organizations-tabs .ch-tab {
