}

/* THREE TIERS, and a type scale sized for AAC rather than for the web default. The panel
   was a single sentence with nothing above it, so there was no shape to read: what went
   wrong, what it means, and what to do all arrived at one weight. Title carries the verdict,
   message explains it, and the buttons below are the only thing to act on.
   Measured on the card's darkest stop (#ECF1FA): title 10.70:1, message 6.42:1.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   PX THROUGHOUT, NEVER rem/em. Bootstrap sets `html { font-size: 10px }`
   (node_modules/bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.css:1081), so a rem here is a TENTH of what it
   reads as: this block was written as 1.05-1.75rem and rendered 10.5px to 17.5px — four of
   the five tiers under 14px, which is why the panel looked tiny. Same trap, same fix, as
   `.md-home-boards-picker__load-more-btn` (app.scss:5595). A future edit that "tidies" these
   back into rem will silently shrink the panel by 37%. */
.board-load-error__title {
  font-size: 28px;
  font-weight: 700;
  line-height: 1.2;
  margin: 0;
  max-width: 520px;
  color: #1B365D;
}

.board-load-error__message {
  /* The explanatory tier, separated from the title by weight and colour rather than by being
     small — at AAC sizes the supporting line still has to be comfortably readable, which is
     why it is muted only to 0.82 and sits well above the 14px floor. */
  font-size: 20px;
  font-weight: 500;
  line-height: 1.5;
  margin: 0;
  max-width: 520px;
  color: rgba(27, 54, 93, 0.82);
}

.board-load-error__retrying {
  font-size: 17px;
  margin: 0;
  font-style: italic;
}

