   `#inner_header:has(#speak)`, but this one declaration must not be: an engine
   without `:has()` support would drop the whole block and take the anchor with
   it, reproducing the +776px bug, and this repo ships Cordova (Android System
   WebView) and Electron alongside the browserslist targets in config/targets.js.
   Before the control was un-nested the bar anchored it without needing `:has()`,
   so scoping this would make the fix strictly more fragile than what it replaced.
   The eval header carries the same declaration, also without `:has()`, in
   `#speak.md-eval-header .speak-bar__button-list-wrap` (added 2026-05-04,
   0e42a9471, for the quick-assessment layout) -- which is why eval mode never
   showed this bug. This matches that shape.

   This also matches the wrap in templates/brief.hbs, which has no absolutely
   positioned descendants, so the rule is inert there.

   Guarded by tests/integration/speak-bar-anchor-test.js: delete this, or re-scope
   it behind a selector the test does not reproduce, and that test goes red. No
   other CI gate can see it. */
.speak-bar__button-list-wrap {
  position: relative;
}

/* Wrapper for button_list + speak_options: container outline and flex layout; grows when words wrap.
   wrap min-height + chip height + image height are driven by CSS
   custom properties so the bar scales with the user's
   vocalization_height (small/medium/large/huge — `tiny` is a legacy
   alias for small via utils/display_prefs.js). The size-class
   rules below this block (`header.speaking.small`, `.medium`, etc.)
   set the per-size values; this rule's fallbacks reproduce the
   prior hardcoded small/90 baseline so contexts that don't set the
   vars (e.g. the eval header, no size class on header) stay
   unchanged. The +2px on each pair (wrap > chip > img) is the 8+8
