/* Compact variant — the Privacy Commitment paragraph reads at 16px rather than the
   22px display size the Accessibility Statement keeps. Both share
   .la-a11y-display-text, so this modifier is what separates them.

   DOUBLED SELECTOR ON PURPOSE (.la-a11y-display-text.la-a11y-display-text--compact,
   specificity 0,0,2,0): the responsive rules further down the file set
   `.la-a11y-display-text { font-size: 20px }` at <=md and `18px` at <=sm. Those are
   0,0,1,0 but appear LATER, so a lone `.la-a11y-display-text--compact` would tie on
   specificity and lose on source order below 768px. The compound wins at every width
   without needing !important (see the app.scss cascade note in LEARNINGS.md).

