/* ── Switch Languages modal ──────────────────────────────────────────
   Replaces the Bootstrap horizontal-form grid this modal used to carry. The header and its
   close button come from the shared `.la-modal-header` chrome (already in the universal
   header list); the footer is registered in the universal footer alias list above, which is
   what gives it the shared gradient + padding — a `la-*-modal-footer` that is NOT in that
   list silently gets no chrome at all (styling-recurring-problems.md #7).
   The legacy `#languages_prompt .form-group .glyphicon` and `.big_select` rules were DELETED
   rather than left in place: both had zero consumers left repo-wide once the markup changed,
   and a legacy descendant rule that outlives its replacement is exactly how the Share Text
   restyle half-landed (see LEARNINGS 2026-08-27). */
/* The header label. Without this the shared `.la-modal-header-label` base applies, whose
   colour is $brand-honey-bronze (#F2B95A) — measured 1.68:1 on this header's $surface-100
   ground, against the 4.5:1 that 15px/800 text needs. That base is the legacy eyebrow
   treatment; every modernised modal overrides it the same way (devices :38468, add-app,
   colors, features, big-button), and this modal was simply missing the override rather than
   needing a new colour. var(--md-ink) is #111A2E => 17.5:1. `text-transform: uppercase` is
   deliberately left inherited: none of the sibling modals reset it, so the eyebrow keeps its
   house form and only the contrast changes. */
/* The icon TILE. There is no base `.la-modal-header-icon` rule — every modal's tile lives on
   its own modifier (`--app` :38407, `--devices`, `--colors`, `--valet`), so a modifier with no
   rule renders as a bare glyph with no box and no flex-shrink, which is why this one sat flush
   against the title. Verdigris tint to match the globe's own accent stroke. */
.la-modal-header-icon--languages {
  width: 46px;
  height: 46px;
  border-radius: 14px;
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  background: rgba(42, 157, 143, 0.1);
  border: 1px solid var(--md-line);
  flex-shrink: 0;
}

.la-languages-modal-wrap .la-modal-header-label {
  margin: 0;
  font-weight: 900;
  font-size: 20px;
  letter-spacing: -0.2px;
  color: var(--md-ink);
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  min-width: 0;
  /* Centred title. The header is `justify-content: space-between` with three children, and
     this one takes the space between the 46px icon tile and the 48px close button — so
     centring the text inside it lands within ~1px of the modal's true centre without having
     to take the close button out of flow. */
  text-align: center;
}

/* Half the shared 28px. `.modal` qualifier is load-bearing: the universal end-of-file
   `.modal .la-modal-header` rule is (0,2,0) and sits LATER, so an unqualified wrapper rule
   is also (0,2,0) and loses its vertical padding entirely. (0,3,0) makes this authoritative.
   Same pattern as `.modal .la-share-text-modal-wrap .la-modal-header`. */
.modal .la-languages-modal-wrap .la-modal-header {
  padding-top: 22px;
  padding-bottom: 22px;
}

.la-languages-modal-body {
  padding: 20px 24px;
}

.la-languages-form {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 18px;
}

.la-languages-desc {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 15px;
  line-height: 1.6;
  color: var(--md-ink);
}

/* Label above control rather than the old 4/8 column split: at the widths this modal is
   actually shown, a side label left the select under ~180px and clipped long endonyms. */
.la-languages-field {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 8px;
}

.la-languages-field__label {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
