/* Width only. `@select_class` lands on BoundSelect's OUTER `.bound-select` wrapper, not on a
   `<select>` — the visible control is `.bound-select__trigger`, which already carries the
   modern skin (44px min-height, its own chevron, focus ring). Restyling it from here would
   fork one modal's select from every other one for no reason, and the first draft of this
   rule did exactly that by aiming padding and borders at the wrapper, where they did nothing.
   Menu clipping is likewise already handled: `.modal-content .bound-select__list` (:98132)
   flow-positions the list for every modal (styling-recurring-problems.md #1). */
.la-languages-select {
  width: 100%;
}

/* Segmented pair, shown when the board offers exactly two languages. Equal flex basis so
   neither language's name dominates, and wrapping text rather than the old
   `max-width: 50%; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis` inline style, which truncated
