  margin: 0 auto;
  color: var(--md-ink);
}

/* ACCOUNT-SECTION PAGE HEADER: icon + title on one rule, shared by the Subscription and
   Supervision pages (supervision joined 2026-09-21, requested — "match the subscription
   header"). Listed together rather than copied so the two cannot drift; a third page wanting
   this header adds its selector here rather than a fourth scale of its own.
   TRAININGS JOINED 2026-09-25 (requested: "add a Training header and icon just like the Goals
   page has"). It had a BARE `<h2>` and no icon — the only page in the section with neither.
   IT JOINED HERE RATHER THAN COPYING `.md-goals__header`, which is a byte-identical copy of the
   block below made before this family existed. That copy is also why Goals renders a 25px title
   while everything here renders 26: `.md-goals__title` sets `font-size: 2.1rem` with no
   `!important`, so it loses outright to `h2 { font-size: 25px !important }` (:4039) and its
   declared value never applies. Folding Goals in here would fix that and cost it 1px; left
   alone deliberately, since nobody asked for Goals to change.
   The `> svg` sizing lives here so a consumer does not have to borrow
   `.md-extras-card__svg-icon` from the extras grid to get 28px. Subscription still carries
   that class in its markup and the values are identical, so nothing changes for it. */
.md-billing__header,
.md-supervision-page__header,
.md-user-summary__focus-head,
.md-stats-main__focus-head,
.md-lessons__header {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 14px;
  margin-bottom: 28px;
  padding-bottom: 18px;
  border-bottom: 1.5px solid rgba(17, 26, 46, 0.12);
}

.md-billing__header > svg,
.md-supervision-page__header > svg,
.md-user-summary__focus-head > svg,
.md-stats-main__focus-head > svg,
.md-lessons__header > svg {
  width: 28px;
  height: 28px;
  flex: none;
}

/* `.md-user-summary__focus-head` is the ACCOUNT page's Focused-View-only header
   (templates/user/index.hbs gates it on `effectiveLayout`, so it is never built in Gentle,
   where the hero serves instead). It joined this family on 2026-09-21: it had been using
   `.md-card__title` at 18px, the only page in the section not at 25px/900, and carried a
   subtitle none of its siblings has. Joining here also gives it the family's border-bottom,
   which replaced the separate `md-card--boards__divider` element it used to render. */
.md-billing__title,
.md-supervision-page__title,
.md-user-summary__focus-title,
.md-stats-main__focus-title,
.md-lessons__title {
  margin: 0;
  /* 26px, set in px on purpose (requested 2026-09-24). This was `2.1rem`, which is 21px at this
     app's 10px root -- and it was NOT what rendered either: the heading is an `<h2>`, and a bare
     `h2 { font-size: 25px !important }` in this same file beats any class selector without one.
     Traced in the browser rather than guessed; the `!important` here is MATCHED to that rule,
     not added to win a specificity race. An absolute value says what it means and cannot drift
     with the root size, which is what the rem was buying and what this heading does not want. */
  font-size: 26px !important;
  font-weight: 900;
  letter-spacing: -0.2px;
  color: var(--md-ink);
}

