}

.md-logs__header {
  /* COLUMN, unlike the other account-section headers: this one carries the page's filter
     controls below the title (requested 2026-09-21), where the rest carry a title alone.
     `align-items: flex-start` because a stretched column would make the links span the full
     width and put their hover targets miles from the text. The 10px gap is title-to-links,
     deliberately tighter than the 14px icon-to-title gap the row-based headers use. */
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 10px;
  margin-bottom: 28px;
  padding-bottom: 18px;
  border-bottom: 1.5px solid rgba(17, 26, 46, 0.12);
}

/* GENTLE: THE HEADER ARRIVES FROM THE LEFT, ITS LINKS FROM THE RIGHT, AND BOTH FINISH CENTRED
   (requested 2026-09-21: "make the header and links below it move in from the left and right
   from the page, respectively, centered when they are done (like the other pages on gentle
   view)").
   Half of this already existed: `.md-logs__header` carries `md-slide-in-from-left` further
   down this file, so only the links were missing their half of the movement, and the block was
   left-aligned rather than centred like the other Gentle pages' headers.
   `align-items: center` rather than `text-align` alone: this is a flex column, so centring the
   ITEMS is what moves the links; `text-align` then centres the title's own wrapped lines. It
   does not stretch them, so the links keep their shrink-wrapped hover targets -- which is the
   reason the base rule gives for choosing `flex-start` over `stretch`, and it still holds.
   Gentle only, as asked; Focused keeps the left-aligned header. */
body:not(.ll-layout-focused) .md-logs__header {
  align-items: center;
  text-align: center;
  animation: md-slide-in-from-left 0.75s cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.46, 0.45, 0.94) both;
}

.md-logs__title {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 2.1rem;
  font-weight: 900;
  letter-spacing: -0.2px;
  color: var(--md-ink);
}

/* Was `.md-logs__title a`, when the filter links lived inside the <h2>. They are a sibling
   of it now, so the selector followed them rather than being duplicated. */
/* The links' half of the movement above. Same duration and easing as the header's
   `md-slide-in-from-left`, so the two sides meet rather than racing. */
body:not(.ll-layout-focused) .md-logs__filters {
  animation: md-slide-in-from-right 0.75s cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.46, 0.45, 0.94) both;
}

/* ARRIVED FROM THE UPDATES PILL-NAV — centre the page title and the filter links under it
   (requested 2026-09-22). Keyed on `.md-main--updates-arrival` (templates/user.hbs), set from
   the same `homeNavContext` the nav choice uses, so this cannot reach the logs page opened
   from the account rail, nor any other account-section page.

   `align-items`, NOT JUST `text-align`. A first attempt set `text-align: center` on the title
   and the links and did nothing: `.md-logs__header` is `display: flex; flex-direction: column;
   align-items: flex-start` (~51721), so its children shrink-wrap to their content at the left
   edge and there is no spare width for text-align to centre within. Overriding the cross-axis
   alignment is what actually moves them; text-align then centres the wrapped lines of a long
   title. Both are needed.

   Not scoped to Focused View: the marker describes the ARRIVAL, not the view. It is a no-op in
   Gentle, where `body:not(.ll-layout-focused) .md-logs__header` already centres — so this
