  /* SLIGHT GLASSMORPHISM (requested), the same treatment the speak/nav controls wear, via
     the shared mixin so the three toolbars cannot drift. Declared INSIDE this rule rather
     than as a later sibling because both would otherwise set `box-shadow` at identical
     specificity with `!important` and the outcome would rest on source order -- the trap
     that silently dropped the ring from every `#nav_header` control the first time round.
     Nested last, the mixin's shadow simply replaces the one above it.
     `:not(.dropdown-menu *)` keeps it off the dropdown's menu items: those sit on a white
     panel, not on the dark bar, so a white ring would be invisible on them and they are not
     controls on the bar in the first place.
     Both fills were measured against the bar: the shared btn-default fill goes from 2.93:1
     -- under the 3:1 WCAG 1.4.11 minimum for a UI boundary -- to 4.72:1 with the ring, and
     the lighter `.btn-info` paint toggle from 6.44:1 to 7.84:1. No fill is altered, so the
     toggle's dark `#18202C` ink keeps its 7.83:1. */
}
