  box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2) !important;
  /* Bounded so it cannot fight the hide that folds Exit Boards into the hamburger. Once
     nested, this selector resolves to the SAME specificity as that hide and sits ~65,000
     lines later, so an unbounded `display: inline-flex !important` won on source order and
     the button never disappeared. Only `display` needs the bound.

     THE BOUND IS 461px, NOT 641px (fixed 2026-09-22). It matched the old hide, which was at
     640px for both board views; board-alt's hide moved to <=460px when board-alt stopped
     collapsing early, so between 461px and 640px the button was still SHOWN but was no
     longer `inline-flex`. That silently broke its children: the icon is `height: auto` with
